    {
      "candidateId": "mv.item.material-properties.b8bcffe2",
      "proposedType": "item",
      "proposedName": "Material Properties",
      "summary": "Each material should have specific stats or traits that affect how it's used in the game. Some common properties include: - Hardness: A measure of the materialʼs resistance to damage or wear (important for armor, weapons, and durability). You can use a hardness scale (e.g., 1-10), where 1 is soft materials like cloth and 10 is materials like diamond. - Durability: Determines how long a material can last before it breaks or degrades. - Weight: Impacts movement speed, encumbrance, and portability. Heavier materials like iron may slow characters down or reduce mobility. - Flexibility: Important for materials used in tools or armor. More flexible materials might be better suited for specific types of items, such as leather for light armor. - Crafting Difficulty: How hard it is to work with the material. More exotic materials may require special skills, tools, or knowledge to craft effectively. - Magical Conduction: Determines if the material can hold enchantments or be used in spellcasting. Some materials may be better conduits for magic.",
      "source": {
